opening='A monastery steward is the resident officer who handles a monastery’s practical affairs and answers for the institution in ordinary encounters.'
body='The role appears beside the teacher and assembly rather than as another name for the abbot. Mazu’s steward asks after his illness; Yaoshan’s steward carries the assembly’s request for instruction. Linji questions a steward returning from selling the monastery’s yellow rice. At Wutai a steward asks whether Huihui bows to another or to himself; in the Pei Xiu case the steward answers for a temple’s wall image, and another temple steward answers an official about its protector image. The Danxia case makes the office’s custodial stake comic and sharp: Danxia burns a wooden buddha, and the steward who objects is said to lose his eyebrows. The Chan bend is the practical office entering famous public cases as the institution’s immediate custodian and interlocutor.'
